                <pb facs="0828" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg708"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Barrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis instructs Mr. Barrett to ask the Government of Panama whether our
                    diplomatic and consular representatives may exercise their good offices, when
                    occasion requires, in behalf of Chinese subjects as requested by the Chinese
                    Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
